      <activity id="2bd131d8-d653-5828-b86e-f08c58cf078e" activityNameId="ae0f27d9-dae4-5e25-85ff-3f3e4ec659fc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Hard sandstone, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Hard sandstone, at plant
The densitiy of hard sandstone is 2500 kg/m3. This equals a facade tile of 8.4 m2 with a thickness of 0.12 m.;
UUID: cd25aa92-3398-3056-8806-b36688ca430a
This data set includes the material and energy input to produce 1 m3 of hard sandstone as facade tile. The system boundary is the gate at the factory. Transport to the factory is included, but not the transport to the regional storage or the construction site. Wood poles are used for storing the stone tiles.
Location: Data for Switzerland
Technology: none
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 2500 m3
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cd25aa92-3398-3056-8806-b36688ca430a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
